{# THE ROSTER'S BLOCK ON A POST'S CONFIGURE CARD — the four columns this
   module owns, read-only.

   ONE PLACE IT IS EDITED, TWO DOORS ONTO IT. The editor is the module's own
   Watches section; this is the other door, and it links there rather than
   growing a second form. A second editor would be a second validation and
   eventually a second answer.

   Rows only: the card and its heading are the area's. #}

<div class="rset">
    <span class="lb"><b>Expects</b><em>named watches</em></span>
    <span class="ct">
        {%- for key in watch.expects %}
            <span class="r-sh on"><i></i>{{ (shifts[key]|default(key))|lower }}</span>
        {%- else %}
            <span class="r-sh">no watch</span>
        {%- endfor %}
    </span>
    <span class="why">A post that declares none is never counted, never late and never a hole &mdash; only offline.</span>
</div>

<div class="rset">
    <span class="lb"><b>Silence</b><em>late, then offline</em></span>
    <span class="ct"><span class="unit">{{ watch.silenceWindowMinutes }} min / {{ watch.offlineAfterMinutes }} min</span></span>
    <span class="why">A gate that never closes and a rim post reached once a fortnight cannot share one window.</span>
</div>

<div class="rset">
    <span class="lb"><b>Catchment</b><em>what makes a claim verified</em></span>
    <span class="ct"><span class="unit">{{ catchmentM ? catchmentM ~ ' m' : 'none set' }}</span><span class="unit">pool {{ pool }}</span></span>
    <span class="why">Changing it re-derives every past day, because a state is never stored.</span>
</div>
